{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01V3eDCDPJ6xy28i49MD4B7N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote **`answers/06-009-bias-variance-tradeoff.md`** covering:\n\n- **Concept:** Error = Bias² + Variance + Irreducible Noise decomposition\n- **Mechanism:** Learning-curve diagnostic table (both high → high bias; large train/val gap → high variance), levers by failure mode (capacity for bias, data/regularization for variance)\n- **Example:** Random Forest as a variance reducer on a churn dataset (99%/78% → 94%/89%), plus LoRA rank reduction for fine-tuning overfitting\n- **Double-descent caveat:** Over-parameterized LLMs defy the classical U-curve, but the tradeoff still bites in small-data fine-tuning regimes\n- **Pitfalls:** \"More data always helps\" misconception, regularization-as-always-beneficial, missing double-descent for LLMs\n- **Cross-links:** Regularization (Q16), imbalanced datasets (Q11), model debugging (Q3)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":69076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":348,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d9b885c-173d-4851-9853-6a05347a70db","uuid":"bd100e49-09aa-4271-a6dd-26f3df5863da"}
